s-section images of your retina. It can detect early signs of eye conditions such as glaucoma, macular degeneration, and diabetic retinopathy — often years before symptoms become noticeable. Many optometrists recommend it as a valuable baseline for patients over 25, particularly those with a family history of eye disease. While it is an additional cost on top of the standard test, it provides a much more thorough picture of your eye health."}]}]]}],"$L33","$L34","$L35","$L36","$L37"]}]]}]
